  "worked_solution": "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{3}-19{t}^{2}+13) \\\\  & =18{t}^{2}-38t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(18{t}^{2}-38t) \\\\  & =36t-38\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the time when the acceleration is $a=70,$ we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}70 & =36t-38 \\\\ 36t & =108 \\\\ t & =3\\,\\text{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the time when the acceleration is $a=70\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ is $3$ seconds.",
